From: Akisaira <akisaira@outlook.com>
Subject: [PATCH] Input: himax-spi: narrow default track_dist2_max from 420^2 to 115^2 (~12 mm)

hx_track_contacts() retains lifted tracks for track_lost_frames (3 frames,
~25 ms) and matches new contacts within track_dist2_max of the predicted
position. The previous default of 420^2 (~44 mm) caused rapid alternating taps
from two fingers within 44 mm to be merged into the lifted track as a pointer
move instead of registering a new touch down.

Lower the default track_dist2_max to 115^2 (~12 mm), which covers the 99.9th
percentile of single-finger frame-to-frame prediction error (6.1 mm) while
preventing adjacent alternating taps from being swallowed.

Origin: local
Upstream-Status: Pending
---
diff --git a/drivers/input/touchscreen/hx-algo.c b/drivers/input/touchscreen/hx-algo.c
index 6de0bfe80..a1eff6de0 100644
--- a/drivers/input/touchscreen/hx-algo.c
+++ b/drivers/input/touchscreen/hx-algo.c
@@ -23,8 +23,15 @@
 /*
  * Default tracking constants — exposed through hx_algo fields so they can
  * be overridden at runtime via sysfs without reloading the module.
+ *
+ * A contact within sqrt(HIMAX_TRACK_MATCH_DIST2) of a track's predicted
+ * position (1 unit = 0.104 mm) is taken as the same finger.  A finger stays
+ * within about 6 mm of the prediction from one frame to the next; a wider
+ * radius lets a finger landing near one that has just lifted (whose track
+ * lingers for HIMAX_TRACK_LOST_FRAMES) take over that track, and the tap is
+ * lost.
  */
-#define HIMAX_TRACK_MATCH_DIST2   (420 * 420)
+#define HIMAX_TRACK_MATCH_DIST2   (115 * 115)
 #define HIMAX_TRACK_LOST_FRAMES   3
 #define HIMAX_NEW_TOUCH_DEBOUNCE  2
 
